      "content": "I guess, but it feels like the \"innovation\" you're talking about is mostly just people using art as a platform for activism. If a piece is only \"valuable\" because it makes a social commentary, does it even deserve to be called art anymore? It seems like we're replacing actual talent with whoever has the loudest or most popular political stance.",
